I am finished at work.
I walk down the pedestrian street.
The wind is still very cold.
I see a large clothing shop.
The shop is very bright.
I go into the shop.
It is wonderfully warm in here.
A shop assistant stands behind the register.
She looks at me and smiles.
"Hello," she says.
"Hello," I answer.
"I am freezing a lot," I say.
"I only have a thin jacket on."
"I would like to find some warm things."
The shop assistant smiles again.
"It is also very cold today," she says.
"We have many thick sweaters."
"We also have warm winter clothes."
"You just take a look," she says kindly.
"Many thanks," I answer.
